<CaseLayout title="Volleyball performance" eyebrow="04 / VOLLEYBALL · DEVELOPMENT & CHEMISTRY" heading="TURN PRACTICE INTO PERSPECTIVE." description="A browser-based workflow that turns practice and game exports into player comparisons and setter–hitter insights." role="Data ingestion, session storage, analytical comparisons, and interactive dashboard workflows." status="Working browser-based dashboard" stack="JavaScript · Plotly · IndexedDB · CSV / XLSX">
  <section id="question"><h2>The numbers need context.</h2><p>A practice export is a starting point. Comparing players across different roles, volumes, and session types requires care before a percentage becomes a coaching insight.</p><p>The volleyball tool brings sessions into one workflow, keeps the data locally in the browser, and makes the context behind comparisons visible.</p></section>
  <section id="approach"><h2>One workflow, from import to insight.</h2><ol class="case-process"><li><strong>Import and merge sessions.</strong><p>Parse CSV and spreadsheet exports, reconcile session data, and persist datasets in IndexedDB.</p></li><li><strong>Compare with the denominator in view.</strong><p>Use volume-weighted metrics, role-specific comparisons, and minimum-sample guards.</p></li><li><strong>Explore the relationships.</strong><p>Inspect setter analysis, setter–hitter chemistry, player development, and practice-to-game comparisons in Plotly views.</p></li></ol></section>
  <section id="evidence"><h2>A working, inspectable product.</h2><p>The dashboard implements browser ingestion, persistent local datasets, session merging, and analytical views. The value of the workflow is its continuity: a coach can move from an export to a particular player or pairing without rebuilding a spreadsheet each time.</p><a class="button button-dark" href="https://bryanhkwan.github.io/volleyball-dashboard/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Explore the live dashboard ↗</a></section>
  <section id="limitations"><h2>Respect the sample.</h2><p>A small number of attempts can make an apparent difference look more meaningful than it is. The interface uses sample guards and contextual comparisons, but the output still requires domain judgment.</p><p>Team datasets remain separate from this portfolio. Predictive modeling and other roadmap items should be evaluated as future work, rather than assumed current capabilities.</p></section>
  <section id="artifacts"><h2>Follow the workflow.</h2><div class="resource-links"><a class="button button-dark" href="https://bryanhkwan.github.io/volleyball-dashboard/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open dashboard ↗</a></div><p class="resource-caption">Datasets stored by the dashboard are local to that browser and device.</p></section>
</CaseLayout>
